  "body": "What happens: the GUI sets the post options (Skip pauses and homes, Output one-file-per-operation, Threading, End units) through the undoable `SetPostOptions` (document) and `SetSetupPostOptions` (a setup's own, #389), but the MCP server has no tool for either - nothing under `crates/app/src/mcp/` names `PostOptions`. An agent cannot read or change what a program posts with.\n\nExpected: a `set_post_options` tool (and a read in its result or a `get_post_options`) taking the option fields and an optional `setup`: with `setup`, that setup's own options (`SetSetupPostOptions`); without, the document's (`SetPostOptions`) - stated explicitly, as `load_machine` does, so an agent always names its target (no implicit routing, so no #1526-style bleed). Plus a way to make a setup follow the document again (`setup` + `follow: true`), and the camcraft-mcp skill row.\n\nEvidence: found while fixing #1526 (GUI post options bled from Setup2 into Setup1). The MCP path has no bleed only because it has no tool. #1390 plans an MCP `set_post_options` for its Explain switch; this issue is the base tool for the existing options, which #1390 can extend.\n\nDone means: an MCP test sets an option on Setup2 with `setup`, Setup1's resolved options are unchanged, undo restores; a call without `setup` sets the document's; the camcraft-mcp skill lists the tool.\n\nRelated: #1526, #1390, #389.\n",
